From 4d5a15617f2ff75cb56e2b4666cf7176b12e33a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Schmitz <jan.schmitz@whu.edu>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 10:21:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix stored XSS in media/composer tag inputs (Alpine x-data)

User-supplied tag JSON was rendered into Alpine x-data attributes with
|safe, letting an authenticated user break out of the attribute and
execute scripts on any viewer of the asset/composer/CSV-mapping pages.

Add an apps.common json_attr template filter that HTML-escapes the
serialized JSON, and apply it at all three attribute-context call sites.
Harden the two media-tag write endpoints with a _normalize_tags helper
(max 25 tags x 100 chars, list-of-string validation, 400 on bad input).
Tag string content is intentionally not stripped server-side -- the
render-time escape is the security boundary.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
